{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498210-ancestor-spirits-tribal-land","id":1498210,"title":"Ancestor Spirits & Tribal land","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-28T08:20:05-08:00","id":1498210,"title":"Ancestor Spirits & Tribal land","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> That's a question I've had in the back of my mind for a while and I've been hesitating for a while. Here is all the different info I have gathered, but please note that it's all interpretation sometimes from stuff I've read a while ago.<br /> <br /> We have two tribes that have lost access or simple lost their tribal land and by extension their ancestor spirits : The Silent Strider and the White Howler (and I think we can extend that to the Croatan, maybe bunyip but I'm less sure about them). For the first one it's all due to Sutekh's curse and the second it's more an interpretation. Since the WH have their tribal homeland mostly corrupted and there is so few information on them nowadays I've always felt like it made sens their ancestor spirits were probably destroyed/enslaved by the bsd one way or another.<br /> <br /> There are a few tribe that do not have access to their ancestor spirits but that's related to the evolution of the tribe and their belief : The Glasswalkers and the Bones Gnawers.<br /> <br /> My takes from that is that if there is a link it's that Ancestor spirits go to their tribal lands when they are not called upon, or residing inside a caern (or something else that could be an exception).<br /> <br /> What you guys think ? How does it work in your setting ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T14:10:59-08:00","id":1498229,"title":"","content":"The Revised Silent Strider tribebook and the Rage across Egypt sourcebook point to the fact that the ancestors and the tribal lands may not actually be gone, and that it might be possible to bring them back. There are even certain Striders that are geting guidance and can access certain ancestors like Shu Horus. These are all parts of the efforts of Wepauwet's tinkering with the Strider bloodlines and quests performed by Strider heroes that have found the realm.<br /> <br /> You see, the Strder homeland has not been destroyed, it is lost and cannot be found, but over the centries, a number of Striders have found it and found only Wepauwet amidst the ruins of their once glorious kingdom. He offered them guidance and sook their help to brign back the rest of the Striders Ancestors back.<br /> <br /> I'd posit that in the Umbra nothing is really gone. And that with enough will and effort you might be able to find that which is lost and be able to utilise it once more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T16:49:59-08:00","id":1498247,"title":"","content":"Tribal Homelands are special domains created by each tribe's totem Incarna. They are filled with spirits and emanations from the totem. The Silent Strider homeland is not &quot;gone&quot; in the sense it is destroyed, but simply &quot;lost&quot; in the Umbra. It is not however completely inaccessible. Use of the level 5 Strider Gift: Gate of the Moon against difficulty 10 allows Striders to find their homeland. Of course that needs to be rolled each time, it isn't that once found a Strider can just keep coming back. Likewise the Croatan tribal homeland can still be visited despite their being no Croatan, as both Wendigo and Uktena have been known to visit there. But it is devoid of inhabitants possibly a result of Turtle's slumber.<br /> <br /> The tribal homeland of the Black Spiral Dancers is a bit stranger. The early books were very unclear about their nature. Umbra 1e seems to think the Howler totem became corrupted, but now it seems clear that Lion was simply displaced and greatly weakened as Bat became the new BSD tribal totem [edit: big mistake, I should have said Whipporwill]. So either Bat somehow took over the tribal homeland from Lion, or in actuality it is an entirely new tribal homeland created by Bat and the old Howler tribal homeland is still out there or possibly merged into the new one. It's probably immaterial, but I think it is a point worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> The exact relationship between Ancestor spirits and the Tribal Homelands is not clear. If we look at the four examples of Ancestor spirits in Axis Mundi, we find different habitats for each spirit. The example Get of Fenris Ancestor spirit usually dwells in a &quot;pocket realm beyond the Get of Fenris homeland&quot; as do other Get Ancestors. The Wendigo example dwells mostly in the Legendary Realm, but for reasons personal to this spirit not in the portion normally occupied by the myths and legends of the Wendigo tribe. The Fianna example is in the area of the Fianna tribal homeland that is near the Arcadia Gateway. There is even a Silent Strider example whose abode is a place beyond the Silent Strider homeland, but can only be reach by first arriving there and following the River of Life and Death so that it leaves the homeland and enters some other Umbral river. Axis Mundi tells us &quot;[Garou] can also encounter [Ancestor spirits] in their abodes in the Umbra. The locations of some of these places are secrets well guarded by the spirits' living kin or by select members of a caern.&quot;<br /> <br /> So this tells me that Ancestor spirits aren't necessarily &quot;native&quot; to the tribal homelands, and often make their abodes in strange realms, sometimes unique to that spirit or a group of Ancestor spirits in general. But they can be encountered naturally in the tribal homelands as well as in other places. Since the nature of Ancestor spirits is not clear (are they a kind of ghost? an ancestral memory of the tribe or Garou? a special spirit created to fulfill a specific role? something else?), I think it is OK for them to be somewhat mysterious and enigmatic.<br /> <br /> Like all spirits they actually have an ephemeral body, and therefore can wander from place to place in the Umbra if they want. I'd just make their appearance at any part of the umbra that makes sense. A Fianna ancestor might be found in Arcadia Gateway, but a Bone Gnawer ancestor wouldn't be. Likewise a Get Ancestor might chose to visit Battleground at times. Tribal homelands, the Legendary Realm, and even Pangea are probably the most likely realms that Ancestor spirits of most tribes could be in. Some rare few Ancestors might even be dwelling in the Summer Country. And I believe some do serve as caern totems so there isn't any reason why they cannot be in the Penumbra. They probably all have an &quot;abode&quot; where they will go to slumber if their Essence is discorporated, but whether that is where they are &quot;normally&quot; found, or somewhere else undefined, who knows?<br /> <br /> The fate of the Silent Strider ancestor spirits is more mysterious, but they still seem to exist but are somehow more &quot;distant&quot; and therefore inaccessible as a result of Set's curse. The fate of Ancestor spirits from the fallen tribes - Bunyip, Croatan, and White Howlers are more enigmatic. I can't remember any mention of them in a sourcebook although I can easily be wrong. There are &quot;Ghost Bunyip&quot; in Rage Across Australia, but it's not clear if these are Ancestor spirits, or a special kind of spirit (one of the many strange things concerning the Bunyip is that they seemingly allowed the Garou to slaughter them without resistance out of a desire for peaceful non-violence, but their &quot;spirits&quot; are extremely angry and seek revenge).<br /> <br /> Axis Mundi is a wonderful sourcebook that has a lot of amazing details buried within it. I recommend it without hesitation for every WtA storyteller. Just keep in mind it required a deep read to pull everything out, this is not a book to quickly scan. It can answer a lot of questions that STs have about spirits (though sometimes it can be contradicted by later sourcebooks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 12-01-2022, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T01:43:35-08:00","id":1498414,"title":"","content":"Alright thank you so much for all these informations. In my game (White Howler renewal) I felt like since so few information were available about white Howler their ancestor had mostly been abducted, enslaved. With this info I could leave some that were so well hidden that nobody fount them yet. I was reluctant to do this before as I thought that tribal homeland were the main residence for ancestral spirits, being not the case it open up a lot more possibilities. The white Howler were so wild and morbid (I'm following the tribebook and wraith-ish lore) that I would see some ancestors spirits having an abode not far from the cemetery in the pangea, ideally somewhere harsh and cold.<br /> <br /> For the tribal homeland there were lot of different options that have been given. I liked a lot the one saying that while the realm got corrupted by whippoorwill, a hill in the realm stayed pure, as Lion was still alive (joined griffins brood). With the renewal of the White Howler I was thinking to have a sort of twinned realm divided by a huge silver river leading directly to Erebus, with the bsd side and the White Howler side giving an unpleasant feeling of how related the two tribes are, without being the same. Not sure that is the best take but I felt like it had meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T18:45:03-08:00","id":1498588,"title":"","content":"The W20 Umbra book does mention some stuff on the Howlers and their Umbral Homelands and for that matter the Homelands of all Tribes, living and dead. After their fall it was indeed become that of the BSD Homeland, an utterly corrupted place with some parts of it too much even for the BSD. There's also an interesting story of one of last Howlers when he died he became a ghost and after an encounter with some BSD in the Underworld, killed them and purified their ghosts, going on to build a pack of purified BSD ghosts that hunt down the ghosts of BSD and BSD Kinfolk to either redeem them or destroy them.<br /> <br /> Oh and speaking of Erebus, in W20 there's a story of a BSD that was placed in the silver sea, constantly monitored by spirits as the silver burns away the Wyrm's taint. He's been in there for over a decade and no one knows what will happen to him when it's done. Though it does note he is drifting closer to shore lately...<br /> <br /> You know, with the many mentions of the White Howlers in W20 (to say nothing of them getting their own Tribebook), I'm surprised that no one has done a Howler Return scenario for the STV.<br /> <br /> Then again that may just be me and my wishing we had gotten Heart of Gaia all those years ago.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T05:04:16-08:00","id":1498615,"title":"","content":"Yeah there is plenty of &quot;official&quot; hooks that can be used here and there if you dig a bit everywhere, there is a lot of ressources to build something around this tribe. I think the thing is that lot of ST don't even want to hear about this tribe as I've seen a lot of &quot;special snowflake&quot; drama go around the tribe over the years. Since it's a bit controversial they probably wouldn't built on that too much even if the material is out there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T05:48:30-08:00","id":1498617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tanakyelle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1498210-ancestor-spirits-tribal-land?p=1498615#post1498615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah there is plenty of &quot;official&quot; hooks that can be used here and there if you dig a bit everywhere, there is a lot of ressources to build something around this tribe. I think the thing is that lot of ST don't even want to hear about this tribe as I've seen a lot of &quot;special snowflake&quot; drama go around the tribe over the years. Since it's a bit controversial they probably wouldn't built on that too much even if the material is out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say they are controversial. They are just something that's not meant for every campaign and require ST approval.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}